# XCU hash
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# hash is intrinsic (XCU 1.7). The utilities hashed are small scripts the
# test puts in its own directories, found through PATH changes made in the
# test shell. The report format is unspecified; only that it contains the
# pathname of each remembered utility is relied on.

assertion  XCU.hash.001
anchor     utilities/hash.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/hash.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/hash.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       hash with a utility name that is found in PATH exits zero and
           writes nothing; a later hash with no operands exits zero and
           writes output that contains the pathname where the utility was
           found.
test       t/001-add-report.sh

assertion  XCU.hash.002
anchor     utilities/hash.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/hash.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/hash.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       hash -r exits zero and empties the list: a later hash with no
           operands no longer reports the utility.
test       t/002-forget.sh

assertion  XCU.hash.003
anchor     utilities/hash.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/hash.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.4
class      required
since      1992
says       After hash -r the shell searches PATH afresh: a copy of a
           utility placed in an earlier PATH directory than the one it
           was found in before is the one that runs.
test       t/003-research.sh

assertion  XCU.hash.004
anchor     utilities/hash.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       Changing the contents of PATH clears the list of remembered
           locations.
test       t/004-path-change.sh
